{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/IntegratingWithTestFrameworks"},"kind":"article","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/integratingwithtestframeworks"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/assertSnapshot(of:as:named:options:fileID:file:testName:line:column:)","doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotAssertionOptions","doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/MigrationGuides"],"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials","generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The Apple ecosystem currently has two primary testing frameworks, and unfortunately they are not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compatible with each other. There is the XCTest framework, which is a private framework provided","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by Apple and heavily integrated into Xcode. And now there is Swift Testing, an open source testing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"framework built in Swift that is capable of integrating into a variety of environments.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"These two frameworks are not compatible in the sense that an assertion made in one framework"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from a test in the other framework will not trigger a test failure. So, if you are writing a test"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Test"},{"type":"text","text":" macro style, and you use a test helper that ultimately calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"XCTFail"},{"type":"text","text":" under"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the hood, that will not bubble up to an actual test failure when tests are run. And similarly, if"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you have a test case inheriting from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"XCTestCase"},{"type":"text","text":" that ultimiately invokes the new style "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"macro, that too will not actually trigger a test failure.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"However, these details have all been hidden away in the SnapshotTesting library. You can simply","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/assertSnapshot(of:as:named:options:fileID:file:testName:line:column:)"},{"text":" in either an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"XCTestCase"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"subclass ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"or","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Test"},{"type":"text","text":", and it will dynamically detect what context it is running in and trigger"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the correct test failure:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["@Test ","func testFeature() {","  assertSnapshot(of: MyView(), as: .image)  \/\/ ✅","}","","class FeatureTests: XCTestCase {","  func testFeature() {","    assertSnapshot(of: MyView(), as: .image)  \/\/ ✅","  }","}"]},{"type":"heading","text":"Configuring snapshots","level":3,"anchor":"Configuring-snapshots"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For the most part, asserting on snapshots works the same whether you are using XCTest or Swift"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Testing. There is one major difference, and that is how snapshot configuration works. There are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"two major ways snapshots can be configured: "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration\/diffTool-swift.property","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration\/record-swift.property","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"diffTool","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property allows you to customize how a command is printed to the test failure","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"message that allows you to quickly open a diff of two files, such as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"http:\/\/kaleidoscope.app"},{"text":". The ","type":"text"},{"code":"record","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property allows you to change the mode of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"assertion so that new snapshots are generated and saved to disk.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"These properties can be overridden for a scope of an operation using the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/withSnapshotTesting(record:diffTool:snapshotNaming:referenceStorage:locale:timeZone:calendar:operation:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"function. In a Swift Testing context","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you can apply the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/Testing\/Trait\/snapshots"},{"text":" trait to either a single test or an entire suite:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SnapshotTesting","","@Suite(.snapshots(record: .failed, diffTool: .ksdiff))","struct FeatureTests {","  …","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This will override the ","type":"text"},{"code":"diffTool","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"record"},{"text":" properties for each test in the suite.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In an XCTest context, the simplest way to do this is to override the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"invokeTest"},{"text":" method on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"XCTestCase"},{"text":" and wrap it in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withSnapshotTesting"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["class FeatureTests: XCTestCase {","  override func invokeTest() {","    withSnapshotTesting(record: .failed, diffTool: .ksdiff) {","      super.invokeTest()","    }","  }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This will override the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"diffTool"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"record"},{"type":"text","text":" properties for each test function."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"UI Testing","anchor":"UI-Testing","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Xcode’s UI testing tools are currently incompatible with Swift Testing. Simply adding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Testing"},{"type":"text","text":" to any UI test target file will cause a compilation error saying that “Testing”"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cannot be found. This complicates using SnapshotTesting in UI test targets because it needs to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"import Testing in order to provide the test helpers mentioned above."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The way in which Xcode disallows importing Testing in UI test targets is via the presence of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"special Swift flag:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["-module_alias Testing=_Testing_Unavailable"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is done so that people do not expect "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect"},{"type":"text","text":" and other Testing tools to work in UI test"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"targets. If you want to use SnapshotTesting in a UI test target, we recommend that you remove"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this flag:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Open your project’s settings and navigate to the settings for your UI testing target."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Search for “Other Swift flags” in the “Build Settings” tab."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Delete the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$(inherited)"},{"type":"text","text":" flag."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Now you can "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SnapshotTesting"},{"type":"text","text":" in UI test targets "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and"}]},{"type":"text","text":" make use of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"assertSnapshot"},{"type":"text","text":". But"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"do remember that you "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"cannot"}]},{"type":"text","text":" use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect"},{"type":"text","text":" or any of the other tools from Swift Testing."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting"]]},"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Integrating with test frameworks","modules":[{"name":"SnapshotTesting"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"Learn how to use snapshot testing in the two main testing frameworks: Xcode’s XCTest and Swift’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"native testing framework.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting/SnapshotTestingConfiguration/diffTool-swift.property":{"title":"diffTool","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"diffTool"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV8DiffToolV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"DiffTool"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration\/diffTool-swift.property","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The diff tool use to print helpful test failure messages."}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/snapshottestingconfiguration\/difftool-swift.property","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting/SnapshotAssertionOptions":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotAssertionOptions","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SnapshotAssertionOptions"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/snapshotassertionoptions","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SnapshotAssertionOptions","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"SnapshotAssertionOptions","abstract":[{"text":"Options that customize a snapshot assertion.","type":"text"}]},"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting/SnapshotTestingConfiguration/record-swift.property":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SnapshotTesting\/documentation\/SnapshotTesting\/SnapshotTestingConfiguration\/record-swift.property","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"record","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV","text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV6RecordV","text":"Record","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/snapshottesting\/snapshottestingconfiguration\/record-swift.property","title":"record","abstract":[{"text":"The recording strategy to use while running snapshot tests.","type":"text"}]},"doc://SnapshotTesting/documentation/SnapshotTesting/withSnapshotTesting(record:diffTool:snapshotNaming:referenceStorage:locale:timeZone:calendar:operation:)":{"title":"withSnapshotTesting(record:diffTool:snapshotNaming:referenceStorage:locale:timeZone:calendar:operation:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"withSnapshotTesting"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"R"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"record"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV6RecordV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Record"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"diffTool"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SnapshotTestingConfiguration"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:15SnapshotTesting0aB13ConfigurationV8DiffToolV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"DiffTool"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam",